 "notes": [
  "Max, 14 Nov 2026: \"I will have an iteration before long\" (08:08 UTC); to the play server's session, \"use r4c until further notice\" (board, sidplay, 15:47 UTC). will said at 08:08 that a new iteration takes Gen X Stu's 2 cores on azure4 by default, round 3 stopping; Max did not object. Prepared and run by will (Gen 9) on azure4.",
  "The bot is the loop session's stu4c-put (configs/loop-bots.json on research/rollout-loop-20261113 at 4488e91d), its gen7 and x8 blocks unchanged: round 4's control net (without the human tables) as its table net and in its rollouts, pure Stu, and blind (x8.blind: told nothing about who sits against it), so no opponent names are needed.",
  "Its net is round 4c's (models/cardplay/stu-net-r4c-20261113, sha256 e4b689c8...; restore.py fetches it). Round 3's Gen X Stu (stu3-ps, configs/round9-genx-stu.json) stays on its own feed.",
  "9a-32, 8s-32 and 71s-32 are configs/round9-cohort.json's entries unchanged, so they are the same actors (identities) as in the Gen 9 cohort. 6-32 is in the roster as the common bidder only.",
  "Deals: fresh, from bridge_harness.corpus.generate with this run's seed (9021, not used by any earlier run). Left out: policy v4.1's and rollout net v1's training families (gen8x-v3-exclusions.json, 50,818), every family of the source corpus, and every family already played on registered feeds (the cohort's list). Round 4's arena sample and the loop's own deals are not listed; they are arena boards and fresh deals of other seeds."
 ],
 "model_note": "Gen X Stu (round 4c, stu4c-put) is pure Stu: no double-dummy search at any trick. Every card, the opening lead included, is chosen by rollouts on Stu's round 4 control net, which is also its table net, with claims, a guaranteed-line guard and mixing among equal cards as in the loop. It is blind: its rollouts are told nothing about who sits against it. It bids as 6-32. Settings are in the bot's gen7 and x8 blocks (bridge_harness/x8_player.py).",
 "interpretation": "Gen X Stu against each opponent in common auctions is card play alone. Before the arena: round 3's Gen X Stu (stu3-ps) was -0.11 +- 0.15 IMPs a board against these three opponents over 699 boards (arena-gen9-genx-stu-azure4-feed, 14 Nov 16:00 UTC); offline, round 4's nets give up 0.0007 to 0.0015 fewer tricks a decision than round 3's (loop README, a42fe6c1). Report common and native conditions separately. Intervals are descriptive and unadjusted for repeated monitoring.",
